(I was made to hit in America)

11
00:00:43,150 --> 00:00:49,060
I was made to hit in America

12
00:00:49,060 --> 00:00:52,730
You are the sun, you are the star

13
00:00:52,730 --> 00:00:54,730
(To me, forever)

14
00:00:54,730 --> 00:00:58,430
You are the sun, you are the star

15
00:00:58,430 --> 00:01:01,660
(To me, forever)

16
00:01:08,510 --> 00:01:14,120
I was made to hit in America

17
00:01:14,120 --> 00:01:16,950
I was made to hit in America

18
00:01:16,950 --> 00:01:19,820
(I was made to hit in America)

19
00:01:19,820 --> 00:01:22,620
I was made to hit in America

20
00:01:22,620 --> 00:01:25,390
(I was made to hit in America)

21
00:01:25,390 --> 00:01:33,270
I was made to hit in America

22
00:02:16,950 --> 00:02:21,450
Gosh, it's noisy...
Oh no, it's started!

23
00:02:21,450 --> 00:02:22,780
Hey, you!

24
00:02:23,620 --> 00:02:27,250
Yikes! I guess we can't
ride the gondola.

25
00:02:28,690 --> 00:02:31,960
They've still got
the band member's story telling.

26
00:02:44,070 --> 00:02:46,130
Hey, it's the kid.

27
00:02:47,180 --> 00:02:48,240
Rikiya-kun!

28
00:02:48,240 --> 00:02:51,910
Didn't think I'd ever see you
standing on that stage.

29
00:02:51,910 --> 00:02:55,250
I didn't expect to see you, either.

30
00:02:55,250 --> 00:02:59,920
I'll be there watching you.
Give it your best shot!

31
00:02:59,920 --> 00:03:01,760
Thank you.

32
00:03:01,760 --> 00:03:04,760
Oh, and give my regards
to Ryusuke-kun too.

33
00:03:04,760 --> 00:03:06,250
How 'bout Chiba-kun?

34
00:03:07,260 --> 00:03:09,600
Hmph!

35
00:03:09,600 --> 00:03:12,090
-That wasn't good.
-Yeah...

36
00:03:15,800 --> 00:03:17,270
Oh, there you are!

37
00:03:17,650 --> 00:03:19,650
Hey! Koyuki!

38
00:03:19,650 --> 00:03:21,820
Maho! When did you get here?

39
00:03:21,820 --> 00:03:24,990
A little while ago.
The grounds are huge!

40
00:03:24,990 --> 00:03:26,320
Yeah, it's quite big.

41
00:03:26,320 --> 00:03:30,660
We'll be performing here...
This stage in the back.

42
00:03:30,660 --> 00:03:33,160
There're three big stages.

43
00:03:33,160 --> 00:03:35,330
Looks like there're
several smaller ones too.

44
00:03:35,330 --> 00:03:36,330
Uh-huh.

45
00:03:36,330 --> 00:03:39,100
Each band plays on each stage
at the same time.

46
00:03:39,100 --> 00:03:41,770
Hmm. Won't the sound be mixed up?

47
00:03:41,770 --> 00:03:45,110
Aw, I wanna see
Husking Bee from 3 PM.

48
00:03:45,110 --> 00:03:48,610
The stages are far from each other
so it won't be mixed up.

49
00:03:48,610 --> 00:03:50,280
There are trees too.

50
00:03:50,280 --> 00:03:52,950
Wow, Oil Octopus is going to play...

51
00:03:52,950 --> 00:03:56,620
-We're going to be on the 3rd stage, at 6:00.
-Wow, Apple will be playing too!

52
00:03:56,620 --> 00:03:57,960
Yeah.

53
00:03:57,960 --> 00:04:01,230
Hey, BECK and Yoshito
are playing at the same time!

54
00:04:01,230 --> 00:04:02,460
Really?!

55
00:04:02,460 --> 00:04:04,960
These two stages are far from each other,

56
00:04:04,960 --> 00:04:07,130
so we can only see one stage.

57
00:04:07,130 --> 00:04:09,300
I would take Yoshito on the main stage.

58
00:04:09,300 --> 00:04:10,700
He's my classmate.

59
00:04:11,130 --> 00:04:13,970
I'm dying to see Malcolm
on the second stage!

60
00:04:13,970 --> 00:04:16,960
-Um, Ryusuke-kun...
-Ryusuke?!

61
00:04:18,980 --> 00:04:21,480
Um, I'd rather not hear about him.

62
00:04:21,480 --> 00:04:22,980
Huh? Is something wrong?

63
00:04:22,980 --> 00:04:27,150
He's been really edgy
since last week...

64
00:04:27,150 --> 00:04:29,640
I haven't seen him since
we argued over the phone.

65
00:04:30,950 --> 00:04:35,660
-Maho, which...
-Koyuki! Good luck!

66
00:04:35,660 --> 00:04:37,630
Actually, we'll be...

67
00:04:39,430 --> 00:04:40,600
Hello?

68
00:04:40,600 --> 00:04:42,060
Ah, Yoshito!

69
00:04:43,600 --> 00:04:46,600
Really? You're staying
at the suite room?

70
00:04:46,600 --> 00:04:48,610
Yeah, we're coming!

71
00:04:48,610 --> 00:04:50,940
See ya, Koyuki-kun!

72
00:04:50,940 --> 00:04:52,280
Yeah.

73
00:04:52,280 --> 00:04:55,610
I wonder which stage
Maho-chan's coming to see.

74
00:04:55,610 --> 00:04:56,780
Hmm.

75
00:04:56,780 --> 00:04:59,180
Ooh, it's cold!

76
00:04:59,180 --> 00:05:01,880
This could stop your heart! Serious!

77
00:05:07,290 --> 00:05:09,990
They're counting the
number of people there.

78
00:05:10,790 --> 00:05:16,630
There is no way we could get a bigger
audience than Eiji's band or Malcolm!

79
00:05:16,630 --> 00:05:18,970
Yeah, the facilities are different too.

80
00:05:19,970 --> 00:05:22,970
That deal you made
with Leon is outrageous!

81
00:05:22,970 --> 00:05:27,980
If we lose this bet, the only
option left is for us to disband.

82
00:05:27,980 --> 00:05:30,640
I wonder if there are any good ideas.

83
00:05:31,820 --> 00:05:34,650
I still believe in the possibility.

84
00:05:34,650 --> 00:05:38,760
What is it with this
"possibility" of yours?

85
00:05:38,760 --> 00:05:40,310
You mean Koyuki's song?

86
00:05:41,490 --> 00:05:42,090
It's the dream.

87
00:05:42,090 --> 00:05:44,080
-Uh...Dream?
-Eek!

88
00:05:44,930 --> 00:05:46,400
That dream we all saw.

89
00:05:47,930 --> 00:05:51,260
That was definitely an omen.

90
00:05:53,940 --> 00:05:58,440
A dream! You idiot!
I never saw such a dream!

91
00:05:58,440 --> 00:06:00,110
Chiba!

92
00:06:00,110 --> 00:06:01,600
-Chiba...
-Uh...

93
00:06:06,450 --> 00:06:11,620
Maybe you weren't meant
to be a part of this band.

94
00:06:19,460 --> 00:06:20,630
"Weren't meant to be
a part of this band?"

95
00:06:20,630 --> 00:06:22,620
What the hell
are you talking about?

96
00:06:24,300 --> 00:06:27,790
Every member is needed in BECK.

97
00:06:28,810 --> 00:06:32,810
Ryusuke, what we saw was just a dream.

98
00:06:32,810 --> 00:06:37,140
It's true this area is littered
'cause the people have no manners...

99
00:06:40,920 --> 00:06:45,920
It's okay, Taira-kun...
The guy who created BECK says so...

100
00:06:45,920 --> 00:06:47,360
So I'll...

101
00:06:47,360 --> 00:06:50,660
-Hey, Chiba! Chiba, wait!
-Dammit!

102
00:06:52,100 --> 00:06:56,770
It really bothered him that he was
the only one who didn't see that dream.

103
00:06:56,770 --> 00:06:58,670
Even the Beatles and the Stones...

104
00:06:58,670 --> 00:07:01,570
...changed their members
right before their debut.

105
00:07:01,570 --> 00:07:05,110
-Chiba cares about this band
more than anyone...
-This isn't a social club!

106
00:07:05,110 --> 00:07:07,270
We can't make it big like that!

107
00:07:11,450 --> 00:07:13,940
Do you really mean that?

108
00:07:15,620 --> 00:07:19,280
If Chiba quits BECK...
I'm quitting too!

109
00:07:22,290 --> 00:07:24,630
Maria seems like a
really aggressive girl.

110
00:07:24,630 --> 00:07:28,470
Oh, her...You better tell
Koyuki to be careful.

111
00:07:28,470 --> 00:07:29,300
Huh?

112
00:07:29,300 --> 00:07:31,960
Maria's a nymphomaniac!

113
00:07:38,410 --> 00:07:40,080
What! Chiba-kun left?!

114
00:07:40,080 --> 00:07:41,410
His whereabouts unknown?

115
00:07:41,410 --> 00:07:44,580
He's turned off his cell phone,
I can't contact him at all.

116
00:07:44,580 --> 00:07:46,750
What about our performance?

117
00:07:46,750 --> 00:07:48,490
Anyway, let's split up
and search for him.

118
00:07:48,490 --> 00:07:51,820
It's 3:00 now,
so we still have 3 hours.

119
00:07:51,820 --> 00:07:53,820
I'll go take a look
at the campsite.

120
00:07:53,820 --> 00:07:55,660
Then, I'll search the stages.

121
00:07:55,660 --> 00:07:57,990
I'll check out the gates.

122
00:08:12,440 --> 00:08:15,110
What a bubbly stage...

123
00:08:15,110 --> 00:08:18,950
My sister's vision of the
Grateful Sound is barely alive.

124
00:08:18,950 --> 00:08:21,120
Seems like there's more
posers than before.

125
00:08:21,120 --> 00:08:23,120
Yeah, but you get to see bands
you wouldn't ordinarily see...

126
00:08:23,120 --> 00:08:25,960
I think it's okay.

127
00:08:25,960 --> 00:08:27,520
Hey, I just saw her panties!

128
00:08:27,520 --> 00:08:29,290
Really?!

129
00:08:33,960 --> 00:08:35,130
I swear!

130
00:08:35,130 --> 00:08:36,790
"Please recycle even if
this station is unmanned."

131
00:08:35,130 --> 00:08:36,790
I swear!

132
00:08:40,070 --> 00:08:41,630
Chiba-kun!

133
00:08:43,240 --> 00:08:46,300
Chiba-kun's things...
Thank goodness.

134
00:08:47,580 --> 00:08:51,080
-Hi, Koyuki.
-Hmm? Maria?

135
00:08:51,080 --> 00:08:54,150
Hey, is it true that guys get high...

136
00:08:54,150 --> 00:08:57,250
...and wanna make love
before the live show starts?

137
00:08:57,250 --> 00:09:01,590
Uh? I don't have time to talk now...
I've got to find...

138
00:09:07,600 --> 00:09:10,930
Hey, Koyuki? What are you doing?

139
00:09:14,600 --> 00:09:17,270
N-no...It's not...Maho!

140
00:09:30,790 --> 00:09:32,280
Chiba-kun...

141
00:09:48,570 --> 00:09:50,810
Chiba-kun...

142
00:09:50,810 --> 00:09:53,640
Where are you, Chiba-kun!?

143
00:09:54,910 --> 00:09:57,980
Mr. Chiba of the Mongolian Chop Squad,

144
00:09:57,980 --> 00:10:00,920
your friends are waiting
for you at the 3rd stage.

145
00:10:00,920 --> 00:10:05,560
I repeat, Mr. Chiba of
the Mongolian Chop Squad...

146
00:10:05,560 --> 00:10:07,760
...your friends are waiting
for you at the 3rd stage.

147
00:10:07,760 --> 00:10:11,660
Maybe...you weren't meant
to be a part of this band.

148
00:10:21,270 --> 00:10:22,940
I'm sorry Taira-kun.

149
00:10:22,940 --> 00:10:25,670
Take care, Koyuki, Saku...

150
00:10:46,230 --> 00:10:50,430
Chiba-kun! I'm sorry,
I made a mistake.

151
00:10:54,740 --> 00:11:00,470
I was planning to go straight home,
but since these guys are here...

152
00:11:07,920 --> 00:11:14,150
Generation 69. If I hadn't met
this band, where would I be now?

153
00:11:24,270 --> 00:11:26,430
Didn't it get a bit chilly?

154
00:11:28,100 --> 00:11:31,270
You think? Wanna eat the pork?

155
00:11:31,270 --> 00:11:34,510
I wonder if BECK's performance
is going to be alright...

156
00:11:58,130 --> 00:12:01,830
She's amazing.
I'm completely her fan now.

157
00:12:02,140 --> 00:12:04,130
Yes, she's the real deal.

158
00:12:04,980 --> 00:12:08,380
But most of the troops are still at the
main stage, or if not, at the second stage...

159
00:12:08,380 --> 00:12:09,980
Can't beat those numbers.

160
00:12:09,980 --> 00:12:11,720
That's absolutely impossible.

161
00:12:11,720 --> 00:12:13,120
To garner more people
than the main stage,

162
00:12:13,120 --> 00:12:14,850
or even the second stage
for that matter.

163
00:12:14,850 --> 00:12:16,750
It would take a miracle.

164
00:12:21,320 --> 00:12:22,330
What's up?

165
00:12:22,330 --> 00:12:23,990
Let's give up.

166
00:12:23,990 --> 00:12:24,660
What?

167
00:12:24,660 --> 00:12:27,330
Eiji's band on the main stage
is booked solid.

168
00:12:27,330 --> 00:12:29,370
Even Malcolm on the second stage,

169
00:12:29,370 --> 00:12:32,340
who's sold over
20 million CDs in the US...

170
00:12:32,340 --> 00:12:36,000
There's no way a band like us on
the third stage can beat those numbers.

171
00:12:37,270 --> 00:12:41,000
And besides, without Chiba,
we can't perform live.

172
00:12:44,610 --> 00:12:46,780
We still have one more hour.

173
00:12:46,780 --> 00:12:49,950
We're searching for Chiba now.

174
00:12:49,950 --> 00:12:52,790
I saw you from the hotel.

175
00:12:52,790 --> 00:12:55,190
What are you doing here
before the stage?

176
00:12:56,960 --> 00:13:00,020
Hey Ryusuke, are you listening? Hey!

177
00:13:01,130 --> 00:13:04,300
You remember what happens
to the loser now, huh?

178
00:13:04,300 --> 00:13:07,600
Yeah, we're having problems
because of that.

179
00:13:07,600 --> 00:13:08,630
Hmph.

180
00:13:12,480 --> 00:13:13,810
You running away?

181
00:13:16,480 --> 00:13:19,150
Yup, I'm more of a pest than I look.

182
00:13:19,150 --> 00:13:22,310
Watch your back, kid.
He really hates you.

183
00:13:28,660 --> 00:13:29,820
Come with me.

184
00:13:31,330 --> 00:13:33,330
I have something for you.

185
00:13:33,330 --> 00:13:35,160
Alright, let's go!

186
00:13:40,270 --> 00:13:43,670
-Let me go! Let me go!
-Hold him down!

187
00:13:57,620 --> 00:13:59,350
Hey, it's cold!

188
00:14:06,960 --> 00:14:08,950
There's no more time left.

189
00:14:17,470 --> 00:14:18,810
Chiba-kun!?

190
00:14:28,150 --> 00:14:30,820
This guy has calmed down
all of a sudden.

191
00:14:30,820 --> 00:14:34,160
Yeah. Malcolm and Belle Ame
are about to start.

192
00:14:34,160 --> 00:14:35,820
Today's main events, huh?

193
00:14:35,990 --> 00:14:38,600
Untie me! I'm going home.

194
00:14:38,600 --> 00:14:39,650
Huh?

195
00:14:57,450 --> 00:15:02,050
If I can't sing from the heart,

196
00:15:02,050 --> 00:15:07,960
then what is this song for...

197
00:15:07,960 --> 00:15:12,660
You're still here, haven't disappeared,

198
00:15:12,660 --> 00:15:18,000
Still going on strong...

199
00:15:28,980 --> 00:15:32,580
Everybody! The ground's
wet and slippery,

200
00:15:32,580 --> 00:15:36,150
so don't push the folks
in front of you!

201
00:15:36,150 --> 00:15:38,920
Then, let me introduce him to you...

202
00:15:38,920 --> 00:15:40,990
Let's call him out here...

203
00:15:40,990 --> 00:15:42,660
All right, here we go...

204
00:15:42,660 --> 00:15:47,150
Yoshito Morozumi!

205
00:15:49,430 --> 00:15:53,770
Hi girls! Are you ready? Okay?!

206
00:15:53,770 --> 00:15:56,330
Morozumi!!

207
00:16:01,440 --> 00:16:06,280
Lying in the bed,
you said, "It's not happen..."

208
00:16:12,120 --> 00:16:14,450
Hey, what's security doing?

209
00:16:15,290 --> 00:16:18,490
We've had injuries
in past performances!

210
00:16:19,300 --> 00:16:21,300
17,000 at the main,

211
00:16:21,300 --> 00:16:23,970
10,200 at the second,

212
00:16:23,970 --> 00:16:26,800
500 at the third stage.

213
00:16:26,800 --> 00:16:30,310
Thanks, man. Keep me posted.

214
00:16:30,310 --> 00:16:31,930
That can't be a good match.

215
00:16:32,480 --> 00:16:36,310
Well, the rain surely fucked up
the equipment on the third stage...

216
00:16:36,310 --> 00:16:38,150
The show hasn't even started.

217
00:16:38,150 --> 00:16:39,640
You may be right.

218
00:16:41,750 --> 00:16:44,480
Hah, these fools are unlucky!

219
00:16:45,420 --> 00:16:48,260
What did you say?!
You're going to withdraw?

220
00:16:48,260 --> 00:16:50,760
It can't be helped.

221
00:16:50,760 --> 00:16:54,100
It won't be a performance
without Chiba and Ryusuke.

222
00:16:54,100 --> 00:16:56,000
Even if we did an
impromptu performance,

223
00:16:56,000 --> 00:17:00,100
it won't be worth a tenth
of our usual show.

224
00:17:00,100 --> 00:17:06,280
That may be true, but what about the 500
people waiting for you out in the rain?

225
00:17:06,280 --> 00:17:10,110
Huh? 500 people? That's amazing!

226
00:17:10,110 --> 00:17:14,280
It's not amazing, compared to
the main and second stages.

227
00:17:14,280 --> 00:17:16,290
They're them, we're us.

228
00:17:16,290 --> 00:17:17,350
That's right!

229
00:17:17,350 --> 00:17:21,620
It doesn't matter how many
Ran and Leon gather together!

230
00:17:21,620 --> 00:17:24,960
You guys replaced the disbanded
band Loud [Crime City].

231
00:17:26,460 --> 00:17:30,300
I can feel you guys are special.

232
00:17:30,300 --> 00:17:33,470
I've been through
3 different bands so far...

233
00:17:33,470 --> 00:17:36,140
2 of which are no longer together.

234
00:17:36,140 --> 00:17:39,970
I don't think BECK has the kind
of chemistry that we used to have.

235
00:17:41,080 --> 00:17:42,200
Taira-kun.

236
00:17:42,750 --> 00:17:45,410
Sato-san, the equipment is almost ready!

237
00:17:47,750 --> 00:17:50,590
500 people...waiting to see us.

238
00:17:50,590 --> 00:17:53,590
Yeah, they're people who've heard
of us through word of mouth.

239
00:17:53,590 --> 00:17:55,690
Honestly, the way things look now,

240
00:17:55,690 --> 00:17:59,260
it might be too hard to meet these
people's expectation of BECK.

241
00:17:59,260 --> 00:18:01,260
Saku, haven't you noticed?

242
00:18:01,260 --> 00:18:05,270
There're several people out there
who always come to our shows.

243
00:18:05,270 --> 00:18:08,600
All the way out here in the mountains,
out in the rain...

244
00:18:14,440 --> 00:18:16,240
Koyuki-kun! Saku-chan!

245
00:18:16,450 --> 00:18:19,280
Wow, Hiromi-chan!
Did you come here by yourself?

246
00:18:20,620 --> 00:18:22,290
You should take a deep breath.

247
00:18:22,290 --> 00:18:23,450
Huh?

248
00:18:23,450 --> 00:18:27,120
That's what I always do
before a tournament.

249
00:18:27,120 --> 00:18:28,790
Oh?

250
00:18:28,790 --> 00:18:34,130
I've never seen both of you
look so uneasy...

251
00:18:39,900 --> 00:18:41,890
Can I...borrow this?

252
00:18:46,410 --> 00:18:48,910
This guitar sounds really great.

253
00:18:48,910 --> 00:18:51,580
Isn't that Jewel's acoustic guitar?

254
00:18:51,580 --> 00:18:54,650
Can I borrow this?

255
00:18:54,650 --> 00:18:58,590
I want to go all out
